<component>
  <section>
    <templateId root="1.3.6.1.4.1.19376.1.5.3.1.3.4"/>
    <code code="10164-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="History of Present illness Narrative"/>
    <title>History of Present Illness</title>
    <text><paragraph>Mr. Freud returns twelve weeks after intake. He stopped smoking on his quit date five weeks ago. In the second week he smoked one cigar after a dinner with colleagues, felt worse for it, and has not smoked since; he did not treat it as a reason to give up. He uses the 21 mg patch each morning and three to five lozenges a day, and takes varenicline 1 mg twice daily. He sleeps well and his mood is steady. Dr. Vasquez-Lindqvist fitted the new obturator this morning, and with it there is no nasal leakage. He has had four speech-language therapy sessions since the last visit. His head and neck surgeon&apos;s yearly examination two weeks ago, with flexible endoscopy, found no recurrence and no second cancer. His pain is 3 of 10. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Element</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Tobacco</td><td>No smoking for five weeks except one cigar in the second week</td></tr><tr><td>Treatment</td><td>Varenicline 1 mg twice daily; 21 mg patch; three to five lozenges a day</td></tr><tr><td>New obturator</td><td>Fitted this morning; no nasal leakage</td></tr><tr><td>Surveillance</td><td>Surgeon&apos;s yearly examination two weeks ago: no recurrence</td></tr><tr><td>Pain</td><td>3 of 10</td></tr></tbody></table></text>

  </section>
</component>

