    <text><list listType="ordered"><item><content styleCode="Bold">Tobacco use disorder, severe, in early remission (F17.290)</content>. Five weeks without smoking after one slip that he handled well. Varenicline is continued beyond 12 weeks to lower the chance of relapse. [S]<list><item>Continue varenicline 1 mg twice daily for at least 24 weeks in total.</item><item>Step the patch down to 14 mg from next week for four weeks, then stop.</item><item>Continue lozenges as needed and quitline calls every two weeks.</item></list></item><item><content styleCode="Bold">History of palatal squamous cell carcinoma (Z85.818)</content>. No recurrence or second primary on the surgeon&apos;s yearly examination. [S]<list><item>Next surgeon&apos;s examination in one year; mouth checked at each visit here.</item></list></item><item><content styleCode="Bold">Hypernasal speech and nasal leakage (R49.21)</content>. Resolved with the new obturator and speech therapy. [S]<list><item>Two more speech-language therapy sessions to finish the course.</item></list></item><item><content styleCode="Bold">Weight loss (R63.4)</content>. Weight 59.8 kg and albumin 3.7 g/dL, both recovering. [S]<list><item>Continue supplements until weight is over 60 kg.</item></list></item></list><paragraph>Protocol monitoring: items the monitoring protocol calls for at this visit. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Domain</th><th>Measure</th><th>Interval</th><th>Status</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Survey</td><td>Tobacco use (cigars a day), readiness and quit date</td><td>Every visit</td><td>Completed today</td><td>No smoking for five weeks except one cigar in the second week; exhaled carbon monoxide 4 ppm (narrative)</td></tr><tr><td>Medication safety</td><td>Varenicline adherence and side effects (nausea, sleep, dreams, mood)</td><td>Every visit; at least 12 weeks, extended to 24 weeks or more</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Taking it twice daily; no side effects now; extended to at least 24 weeks</td></tr><tr><td>Medication safety</td><td>Combination nicotine replacement (patch and lozenge)</td><td>From the quit date for at least 8 to 12 weeks</td><td>Completed today</td><td>21 mg patch for six weeks, then 14 mg for four weeks; lozenges three to five a day; mild redness at patch sites</td></tr><tr><td>Self-management</td><td>Behavioral support (quitline and clinic sessions)</td><td>Weekly calls around the quit date, then every two to four weeks</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Weekly quitline calls around the quit date; now every two weeks</td></tr><tr><td>Self-management</td><td>Relapse prevention</td><td>Every visit</td><td>Completed today</td><td>The slip was reviewed without blame; plan for dinners and travel</td></tr><tr><td>Examination</td><td>Head and neck surveillance examination (mouth, defect and neck)</td><td>Yearly by his head and neck surgeon more than five years after treatment; mouth checked at each visit</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Surgeon&apos;s yearly examination with flexible endoscopy two weeks ago: no recurrence or second primary; mouth healthy today</td></tr><tr><td>Imaging</td><td>Head and neck imaging</td><td>Only for symptoms or signs more than five years after treatment</td><td>Not indicated</td><td>No symptoms or signs</td></tr><tr><td>Examination</td><td>Obturator fit, seal and hygiene</td><td>Every visit</td><td>Completed today</td><td>New definitive obturator fitted this morning by Dr. Vasquez-Lindqvist; good seal</td></tr><tr><td>Examination</td><td>Speech and swallowing (hypernasality, nasal leakage)</td><td>Every visit; speech-language therapy as needed</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Four therapy sessions since the corrective action; normal resonance with the new obturator</td></tr><tr><td>Examination</td><td>Weight and nutrition</td><td>Every visit</td><td>Completed today</td><td>59.8 kg</td></tr><tr><td>Laboratory</td><td>Albumin</td><td>Baseline and at three months while weight is recovering</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Albumin 3.7 g/dL, from 3.4</td></tr><tr><td>Survey</td><td>Pain score and function</td><td>Every visit</td><td>Completed today</td><td>3 of 10, measured before the new obturator was fitted</td></tr><tr><td>Medication safety</td><td>Acetaminophen daily dose (no more than 3,000 mg)</td><td>Every visit</td><td>Completed today</td><td>3,000 mg a day</td></tr><tr><td>Medication safety</td><td>Opioids</td><td>Avoid long-term opioids</td><td>Not indicated</td><td>Not needed</td></tr></tbody></table><paragraph>Goal progress:</paragraph><list><item>Stop smoking cigars completely, at a pace he chooses, using varenicline and nicotine replacement. In progress; target 1930-10-26 [S]</item><item>An obturator that seals and does not rub, so that speech is clear and liquids do not leak into his nose. Outcome by 1930-08-24: Reline at two weeks; new definitive obturator fitted at twelve weeks; speech clear and no nasal leakage [S]</item><item>Pain at 3 of 10 or less without opioids. In progress; target 1930-10-26 [S]</item><item>Regain weight to at least 60 kg with a normal albumin. In progress; target 1930-10-26 [S]</item></list><paragraph>Guideline basis: Initiating Pharmacologic Treatment in Tobacco-Dependent Adults. An Official American Thoracic Society Clinical Practice Guideline (2020); Tobacco Smoking Cessation in Adults, Including Pregnant Persons: Interventions (2021); NCCN Clinical Practice Guidelines in Oncology: Head and Neck Cancers, Version 2.2026 (follow-up and survivorship) (2026); American Cancer Society Head and Neck Cancer Survivorship Care Guideline (2016); CDC Clinical Practice Guideline for Prescribing Opioids for Pain — United States, 2022 (2022)</paragraph><paragraph>Follow-up: Patch step-down from next week. Quitline every two weeks. Two more speech-language therapy sessions. Five-month review in nine weeks with blood count, albumin, kidney function and ALT. Next scheduled visit 1930-09-28: subsequent annual wellness visit. [S]</paragraph></text>

